<para id="RM000001Z0X006X" category="C" type-id="801I2" name-id="940AM-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B2325</dtccode>
<dtcname>Door LIN bus malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000001Z0X006X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000008100000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) detects door bus errors; it performs 1 error detections in 2.6 seconds, and outputs this code when an error is detected 3 times in a row (7.8 seconds). </ptxt>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1" pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="0.99in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="2.62in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="3.47in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B2325</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>When a door bus error is detected 3 times consecutively</ptxt>
<ptxt>(LIN Communication Line Malfunction)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument Panel Junction Block Assembly</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Main Body ECU)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire Harness or Connector</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Power Window Regulator Motor Assembly LH</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Rear) [Power Window ECU]</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Power Window Regulator Motor Assembly RH</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Rear) [Power Window ECU]</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Power Window Regulator Motor Assembly LH</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Front Passenger Side) [Power Window ECU]</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Power Window Regulator Motor Assembly RH</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Driver Side) [Power Window ECU]</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Power Window Regulator Master Switch Assembly</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Driver Side Power Window Switch)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000001Z0X006X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000008200000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162405J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000001Z0X006X_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___000008300000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When using the TaSCAN with the IG OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON and OFF (at intervals of 1.5 seconds or less) until communication between the TaSCAN and the vehicle starts.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the main body ECU is replaced with a new one and the battery negative terminal is reconnected, it enters the IG ON state. Also, when the battery is removed and reinstalled, it returns to the state it was in when the battery was removed.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
